### 5.1 Proof obligations and where they are discharged

| # | Claim | Test |
|---|---|---|
| I1 | Every `d ∈ [0,D)` lands in exactly one `d`-tile, for `D % BD != 0` | `proveDPartition` over `D∈{1,2,5,7,16,17,31,32,33,64,65}`, `BD∈{1,3,4,5,8,16}` |
| I2 | Every query row lands in exactly one row-tile | `proveRowPartition` over ragged `Lq` incl. `1` |
| I3 | Every key column lands in exactly one KV tile; tail clamped | `proveKVTiling` over `Lk` incl. `1` and `BN > Lk` |
| I4 | Every output element has `writeCount == 1` | hard `assert` inside `tiledAttention` for all `(b,h,i,d)` |
| I5 | State updated once per KV tile, ascending, monotone max | structured loop; `mNew = max(m, mTile)` |
| I6 | Bitwise-stable across runs | `sameBits(run1.O, run2.O)` |
